    "published_date": "2026-07-23",
    "summary": "Most React \"state management\" libraries only propagate or cache state updates; they do not truly manage state over time. Real state management requires handling time, order, and conflicts to keep data consistent and reliable. True solutions exist but are not yet common, and we need to rethink how we approach application state beyond current tools.",
