    "published_date": "2026-07-22",
    "summary": "Finland plans to increase its data center capacity by 27 times by 2030, nearly matching its entire national power grid. Big companies like Google control a large part of this growth, but they are reluctant to reduce power use when the grid is stressed. Finland also shares detailed data about these projects openly, which is rare in Europe.",
